From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:48:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] localspl: AddMonitor/DeleteMonitor release the monitor (3298)

CORE review: printing.

Patch 1034 gave a monitor a resident reference that only DeleteMonitor
releases, but AddMonitor kept the reference its own monitor_load took, so
DeleteMonitor never freed the monitor. It stayed in the cached monitor
list under its name, and the next AddMonitor of that name found the cached
entry and reported success without loading the DLL (winspool.drv
info.c:382/392/404 failed). AddMonitor now drops its call reference when
the monitor is resident; DeleteMonitor unloads unconditionally as before.

Test: test/fastaddmon-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_ADDMON_REF).

diff --git a/dlls/localspl/provider.c b/dlls/localspl/provider.c
index 0224650..024169e 100644
--- a/dlls/localspl/provider.c
+++ b/dlls/localspl/provider.c
@@ -2287,7 +2287,15 @@ static BOOL WINAPI fpAddMonitor(LPWSTR pName, DWORD Level, LPBYTE pMonitors)
                 res = FALSE;
             }
             else
+            {
+                /* a resident monitor holds the spooler's own reference (see
+                 * monitor_load); the one taken by this call is not kept, or
+                 * DeleteMonitor could never release the monitor */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ADDMON_REF
+                if (pm->resident) monitor_unload(pm);
+#endif
                 SetLastError(ERROR_SUCCESS); /* Monitor installer depends on this */
+            }
         }
 
         RegCloseKey(hentry);
@@ -2582,12 +2590,10 @@ static BOOL WINAPI fpDeleteMonitor(LPWSTR pName, LPWSTR pEnvironment, LPWSTR pMo
     {
         if (pm->name && !lstrcmpW(pMonitorName, pm->name))
         {
-            /* the spooler's own reference */
+            /* the spooler's own reference, or the one AddMonitor kept */
             if (pm->resident)
-            {
                 pm->resident = FALSE;
-                monitor_unload(pm);
-            }
+            monitor_unload(pm);
             break;
         }
     }
